# AppRinger Skills — Routing & Governance Rule

Workspace rules live in `.agents/AGENTS.md`. Skills live in `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`. Shared modules live in `.agents/shared/`.

Before doing feature, change, bug, analysis, or review work, READ the matching skill file and follow it:

| Intent | Read this file |
|---|---|
| Analyze, fingerprint, & onboard codebase | `.agents/skills/analyze-project/SKILL.md` |
| New backend feature / API / DB / Livewire / Service | `.agents/skills/new-feature-be/SKILL.md` |
| New frontend feature / React / Next.js / Vue UI | `.agents/skills/new-feature-fe/SKILL.md` |
| New mobile app feature / screen (Flutter / RN / iOS / Android) | `.agents/skills/new-feature-mobile/SKILL.md` |
| Reverse engineer, audit, or create project documentation | `.agents/skills/project-documentation-auditor/SKILL.md` |
| Change to an already-documented feature (CR) | `.agents/skills/cr/SKILL.md` |
| Bug, error, wrong behaviour, Root Cause Analysis (RCA) | `.agents/skills/bug/SKILL.md` |
| Code review of a diff / branch / PR / file set | `.agents/skills/review/SKILL.md` |

### Routing Protocol:
- If analyzing/fingerprinting an unfamiliar project or onboarding -> `analyze-project`.
- If building a new backend endpoint/service/worker -> `new-feature-be`.
- If building a new web UI/component/page -> `new-feature-fe`.
- If building a new mobile screen/app feature -> `new-feature-mobile`.
- If creating, auditing, or updating technical docs -> `project-documentation-auditor`.
- If modifying an existing documented feature -> `cr`.
- If fixing a defect or reproducing an error -> `bug`.
- If auditing code or reviewing PRs -> `review`.
- Unsure — ask one clarifying routing question, do not guess.

### Shared Modules:
- `.agents/shared/impact-analysis.md` — run before planning.
- `.agents/shared/grill-me.md` — ask clarifying questions, then STOP for answers.
- `.agents/shared/engineering-standards.md` — AppRinger engineering rules & KK's coding style.
- `.agents/shared/caveman-summary.md` — mandatory final summary.

### Non-Negotiable Core Standards:
1. Impact analysis first.
2. Grill-me before documenting. Never assume business logic.
3. Zero implementation code before explicit plan approval.
4. Multi-tenant isolation on every table with `merchant_id` / tenant scope.
5. SweetAlert2 (`swal()`) — never browser `alert()`.
6. Premium modern UI by default (soft backgrounds, glassmorphism, hover-lifts). No inline styles (`style={{}}`).
7. 100% test coverage with automated tests.
8. Clean workspace — delete temporary scripts immediately.
9. Caveman summary at the end.
